{
 "identity": "bracket_{j+1} = SUM_{t<j} (-1)^t E_2t Q_j(t)/(j-t) A_t/s^{2t}  +  (-1)^j E_2j (n-1-j)! A_j/s^{2j}",
 "mechanism": "Q_{j+1}(t) = Q_j(t)/(j-t) and 1/(j-t) = int_0^1 u^{j-t-1} du, so the step is an integral operator with a POSITIVE kernel (an averaging over smaller lam); at t = j the relation is 0/0 and leaves a boundary term",
 "why_parity": "the boundary term carries (-1)^j: when the next knife j+1 is ODD it enters with a plus and positivity is inherited; when j+1 is EVEN it enters with a minus, which is exactly where a threshold can appear",
